{{Administrative levels and divisions of Balboa sidebar}}

'''Administrative divisions of Balboa''' ({{lang|ca|Divisions administratives de Balboa}}) comprise four levels of sub-national government established under the [[Constitution of Balboa|1974 constitution]] following the country's [[Reunification of Balboa|reunification]]. The structure consists of five [[Provinces of Balboa|provinces]], 106 [[comarca]]s, [[Municipalitats of Balboa|municipalitats]] (municipalities), and — in larger urban areas — ciutats and districtes (cities and districts). Every resident of Balboa resides within a province, a comarca, and a municipalitat; the ciutat and districte levels exist only in certain urban areas.

Balboa is a {{w|unitary state}}, meaning that provincial and local governments derive their authority from the national constitution rather than from inherent sovereignty. Powers are devolved to sub-national governments by constitutional provision, with the national government retaining authority over matters of national concern including defence, foreign policy, the Balboa Canal, immigration, and the currency.

