Provincial governors, comarca commissioners, and mayors are all directly elected by their respective constituencies. All sub-national legislatures are elected by {{w|single transferable vote}} (STV). Provincial, comarca, and municipal elections are held concurrently every four years, separate from the national election cycle.

== Provinces ==

{{main|Provinces of Balboa}}

[[Balboa]] is divided into five provinces, each with an elected provincial assembly and a directly elected governor. The governor serves as the chief executive of the province and is responsible for provincial administration, infrastructure, and the coordination of comarca-level services. Provincial assemblies are elected by STV every four years and have legislative authority over matters devolved to the provinces by the national constitution, including education, health, and provincial transport.

Provincial assembly seats are apportioned by population, with each province receiving a minimum number of seats. Estret Province, the most populous, holds 65 seats; Tramuntana, the least populous, holds 15.

