=== Provincial powers ===

The constitution devolves the following matters to provincial governments:

* Education, including primary and secondary schools, curriculum standards, and the administration of public universities
* Health, including the operation of hospitals and the coordination of the National Health Service at the provincial level
* Provincial transport, including provincial roads, regional rail, and public transit systems
* Land use planning at the provincial level, including the designation of protected areas and provincial parks
* Provincial budget and taxation, including property taxes and provincial surcharges
* Coordination of comarca-level services, including regional planning and the administration of comarca-wide facilities

Matters reserved to the national government include defence, foreign policy, the Balboa Canal, immigration, customs, the currency, national transportation infrastructure (expressways, intercity rail, and airports), and the administration of the [[Twelve Guarantees]].

=== Provincial governors ===

Provincial governors are elected by direct popular vote using a {{w|two-round system}}, concurrent with provincial assembly elections every four years. Governors may serve a maximum of two consecutive terms. The governor appoints a provincial cabinet, subject to confirmation by the provincial assembly.

