== Comarcas ==

{{main|Comarcas of Balboa}}

Each province is subdivided into [[comarca]]s, which serve as the principal intermediate level of government between the province and the municipalitat. Balboa has 106 comarcas in total.

Each comarca is headed by a directly elected commissioner ({{lang|ca|comissari}}), who serves as the chief executive and coordinates comarca-level services including regional planning, comarca roads, and the administration of comarca-wide facilities such as hospitals and secondary schools. Each comarca also has an elected comarca assembly ({{lang|ca|assemblea comarcal}}), whose members are elected by STV from population-proportional constituencies within the comarca every four years. The comarca assembly has legislative authority over comarca-level matters including the comarca budget, land use planning, and the coordination of municipal services. Assembly sizes are proportional to population, with a minimum of 9 and a maximum of 25 members.

