=== Tramuntana ===

{{main|Tramuntana Province}}

[[Tramuntana Province]] is the northernmost and largest province by area, covering 109,881 km² in the highlands of the interior. It is the least densely populated province, with approximately 17.0 inhabitants per km². The province is divided into 27 comarcas, most of which are rural or highland in character. The provincial capital is [[Portblanc]], located in the [[Cala Tranquilla (comarca)|Cala Tranquilla]] comarca on the Shendan coast.

Tramuntana's comarcas range from the densely populated Cala Tranquilla (648,247) to the remote Birú Nord (9,736) in the Tapuya border highlands. Several comarcas — La Serra de Llevant, El Pic del Nord, Els Cims, and Birú Nord — include territory within the [[Gran Presa del Nord]] watershed and the Birú highlands, where indigenous land rights and environmental protections constrain development.

=== Nurra ===

{{main|Nurra Province}}

[[Nurra Province]] covers 70,380 km² in the northeastern coastal region. It is the second-largest province by area and the third-most populous, with 4,487,219 residents. The province is divided into 25 comarcas. The provincial capital is [[Novara]], located in the Sorres Blanques comarca, which is the most populous comarca in the province with 2,198,376 residents.

Nurra's comarcas span the spectrum from the urban Sorres Blanques to the remote Birú Est (16,847) on the Tapuya border. The province includes significant coastline along the Shendan Ocean and several island comarcas, including Illa Petita (5,847) and Les Illes (13,847).

=== Jala ===

{{main|Jala Province}}

[[Jala Province]] covers 65,539 km² in the central-eastern region. It is the second-most populous province, with 8,514,902 residents, and the most densely populated after Estret. The province is divided into 22 comarcas. The provincial capital is [[Sant Bart]], located in the Sant Bart comarca, which is the most populous comarca in the province and one of the most populous in Balboa, with 3,373,731 residents.

Jala's comarcas include major urban centres such as Costabella (1,817,568) and Sant Bart, as well as rural highland comarcas such as Altbirú (28,964) and L'Alzina (50,312). The province includes the petrochemical centre of La Badia (Badia Curta) and the island comarca of Illa Roja (5,107).

=== Estret ===

{{main|Estret Province}}

[[Estret Province]] is the smallest province by area, covering 19,096 km² on the Isthmus of Balboa, but it is the most populous and most densely populated, with 14,523,847 residents and a density of 760.4 inhabitants per km². The province is divided into 13 comarcas. The provincial capital is [[Sant Cristòfor]], the national capital, located in the [[Sant Cristòfor (comarca)|Sant Cristòfor]] comarca.

Estret's comarcas include the Sant Cristòfor metropolitan area, the canal corridor, and the eastern and western coastal regions. The [[International City of Areza]] is an enclave within Estret Province but is not subject to Balboan sovereignty.

=== Migjorn ===

{{main|Migjorn Province}}

[[Migjorn Province]] covers 30,539 km² in the south, along the Aethiopian (eastern) coast of the isthmus. It has a population of 5,834,620 and is divided into 19 comarcas. The provincial capital is [[Sant Llàtzer]], located in the El Delta comarca. Migjorn's comarcas span the canal zone, the southern coast, and the interior highlands.

== Municipalitats ==

The municipalitat (municipality) is the basic unit of local government. Each municipalitat is headed by a directly elected mayor ({{lang|ca|alcalde}}), who serves as the chief executive. Municipalitats are responsible for local services including water, waste management, local roads, primary education, and urban planning. Municipal councils ({{lang|ca|consell municipal}}) are elected by STV every four years. Council sizes are proportional to population, with a minimum of 5 and a maximum of 21 members.

The number of municipalitats within each comarca varies based on population density and geography. Urban comarcas may contain a single municipalitat encompassing the entire comarca, while rural comarcas may contain several municipalitats.

== Ciutats and districtes ==

In larger urban areas, an additional layer of sub-municipal government exists. Most cities with a population over 100,000 are divided into '''districtes''' (districts), each electing a representative to the city council. The city council also includes at-large members elected by the whole city. The mayor is elected directly by the citywide electorate. Smaller cities (under approximately 100,000 population) are not divided into districtes; the mayor and an at-large municipal council are elected by the whole municipalitat.

=== Sant Cristòfor ===

{{main|Sant Cristòfor}}

[[Sant Cristòfor]] is the only city in Balboa to operate a '''ciutat–districte''' system. The mainland municipalitat is divided into eleven ciutats, each with its own elected city council ({{lang|ca|consell de ciutat}}), and each ciutat is further subdivided into districtes, each electing a representative to its city council. This two-tier structure — unique to Sant Cristòfor — reflects the city's exceptional size and complexity.

