== International City of Areza ==

{{main|International City of Areza}}

The [[International City of Areza]] is a permanently neutral international territory located within [[Estret Province]], on the north shore of [[Lake Alvarado]] along the [[Balboa Canal]]. It was established by the [[Treaty of Areza]] (1973) and is governed independently of Balboa. The city is the seat of the [[Adonian Community]] Parliament and hosts the AC Garrison Areza, an international military force. Areza is not subject to Balboan sovereignty and is not included within any Balboan province, comarca, or municipalitat for administrative purposes. The [[International Cooperative Police Force]] maintains a perpetual mandate in Areza.

== Electoral system ==

All sub-national elections in Balboa — provincial assemblies, comarca assemblies, and municipal councils — use the {{w|single transferable vote}} (STV) system. Provincial governors and mayors are elected by direct popular vote; gubernatorial elections use a {{w|two-round system}}, while mayoral elections use a simple plurality in smaller municipalitats and a two-round system in larger cities.

Provincial, comarca, and municipal elections are held concurrently every four years, separate from the national election cycle. This separation ensures that sub-national politics are not entirely subsumed by national party dynamics, though national parties operate at all levels of government.

The [[Third Guarantee]] of the [[Twelve Guarantees]] establishes a minimum seat allocation in the [[National Assembly of Balboa|National Assembly]] for the former [[International Mandate of Sant Cristòfor|mandate territory]] (Estret Province and the Sant Cristòfor metropolitan area), ensuring that the Black and mixed populations of the region maintain guaranteed representation regardless of provincial electoral outcomes.

== Historical development ==

The current four-level administrative structure was established by the [[Constitution of Balboa|1974 constitution]] following the [[Reunification of Balboa|reunification]] of the former [[International Mandate of Sant Cristòfor]] with the Republic of Balboa. Prior to reunification, the two territories had separate administrative systems: the Republic of Balboa used a province–comarca–municipalitat structure inherited from the Volisanian colonial administration, while the mandate territory was administered directly by the [[Adonian Community]].

The 1974 constitution unified the two systems under a single framework, retaining the province and comarca levels while standardising the municipalitat level. The ciutat–districte system was created specifically for Sant Cristòfor to accommodate the city's exceptional size and the complexity of integrating the former mandate territory's governance structures into the national framework.

The [[Twelve Guarantees]], incorporated into the constitution as entrenched provisions, place specific constraints on the administrative structure. The [[Third Guarantee]] guarantees minimum representation for the former mandate territory. The [[International City of Areza]], established by the [[Treaty of Areza]] (1973), was carved from the canal zone as a permanently neutral international territory, removing it from Balboan administrative jurisdiction.

